From: Cidwel Highwind <cidwel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Honour claims that arrived before the sensor was found

The client hash tables are created in bus_acquired_handler(), deliberately
"before DBus is fully exposed", so a Claim can land before name_acquired_handler
has run find_sensors(). handle_generic_method_call() records that claim, finds
driver_type_exists() false, answers OK and starts nothing -- and nothing ever
looks at the table again. The client then waits for readings that never arrive.

The hotplug path in sensor_changes() gets this right for a device appearing
later; only the initial discovery misses it. The D-Bus documentation shipped
with the project promises the working behaviour: that you may claim before an
accelerometer is present and will get data once it shows up.

Seen on a POCO X3 NFC running KWin, which claims the accelerometer 16 ms before
it is found:

    14:12:27.124243  Handling driver refcounting method 'ClaimAccelerometer'
    14:12:27.140022  Found device ... of type accelerometer at SSC accelerometer

Screen rotation then stayed dead -- zero samples in six seconds -- until
something made KWin release and re-claim, such as blanking the screen and waking
it, which produced 176 samples over the same interval.
---
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c	2026-08-28 14:13:53.341401461 +0200
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c	2026-08-28 14:13:22.072837113 +0200
@@ -810,6 +810,24 @@
 		}
 
 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
+
+		/* A client can claim a sensor before find_sensors() has found
+		 * it: the hash tables are deliberately created before the bus
+		 * name is taken, so the Claim is recorded and answered OK even
+		 * though there was nothing to start yet. Nothing revisited that
+		 * table afterwards, so the client waited for readings that
+		 * never came.
+		 *
+		 * Seen on a POCO X3 NFC with KWin, which claims 16 ms before
+		 * the accelerometer is found; rotation then stayed dead until
+		 * something made KWin release and re-claim, such as blanking
+		 * the screen and waking it. */
+		if (g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0) {
+			g_debug ("Honouring %u claim(s) that arrived before the %s device was found",
+				 g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]),
+				 driver_type_to_str (i));
+			driver_set_polling (sensor_device, TRUE);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
